# =============================================================================
# Root .gitattributes
#
# LFS rules MUST be in place before a matching file is first staged. A file
# staged without them is stored as an ordinary blob, and moving it to LFS
# afterwards requires rewriting history. GitHub rejects any blob over 100 MB.
# =============================================================================

# --- Git-LFS -----------------------------------------------------------------
# PDFs (requirement documents, vendor guides) are large, incompressible and never
# diff usefully, so they would cost their full weight in every clone.
*.pdf filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# --- Binary: never diff, never line-ending-normalise -------------------------
*.xlsx binary
*.xls  binary
*.pptx binary
*.docx binary
*.zip  binary
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.webp binary
*.ico  binary

# --- Text: keep line endings exactly as committed ----------------------------
# No '* text=auto': normalising a whole uploaded project on a Windows checkout
# would rewrite every file on first commit and bury real changes in whitespace.
# PowerShell scripts stay CRLF (PS 5.1 is encoding-sensitive); shell scripts LF.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.sh  text eol=lf
